        "set": "answerable",
        "answer": "The main innovation in ScaNN is anisotropic vector quantization [1]. This method quantizes a data point $x_i$ to $\\tilde{x}_i$ [1]. The goal is to make the inner product $\\langle q, x_i \\rangle$ as similar as possible to the original distance of $\\angle q, \\tilde{x}_i$ [1]. This is done instead of selecting the closest quantization centroid points [1].",
