        "answer": "HNSW builds hierarchical layers of small-world graphs [1]. The layers in the middle create shortcuts to speed up search [1]. When searching, HNSW starts at a random node in the top layer and moves down through the layers [1]. Moves in the upper layers can potentially cover a large distance in the data space, while moves in the lower layers refine the search quality [1].",
