        "id": "a13",
        "set": "answerable",
        "answer": "Several biases contribute to the high variance observed in few-shot classification when using LLMs [1]. These biases include: (1) Majority label bias, which occurs if the distribution of labels among the examples is unbalanced [1]. (2) Recency bias, which is the tendency for the model to repeat the label at the end [1]. (3) Common token bias, indicating that LLMs tend to generate common tokens more frequently than rare tokens [1].",
