        "id": "a17",
        "set": "answerable",
        "answer": "The augment-prune-select process for automatically constructing chain-of-thought prompts involves three steps [1]. First, in the Augment step, multiple pseudo-chains of thought are generated using few-shot or zero-shot CoT prompts [1]. Next, the Prune step involves pruning these pseudo chains based on whether their generated answers match ground truths [1]. Finally, the Select step applies a variance-reduced policy gradient strategy to learn the probability distribution over selected examples, while considering the probability distribution over examples as the policy and the validation set accuracy as the reward [1].",
